**Three defects, all false claims about the library, none caught by A2/A3/A6/A7/A8:**

1. **`def-baire-space`** — says the only nowhere-dense/meager notions "available to it" are ℝ-only. False for *nowhere dense*: `def-dense-top` defines it for an arbitrary space with the identical formula, and it is one of this item's own five declared `deps`, cited in the next sentence. The conclusion survives (meager really is ℝ-only); the stated reason doesn't.

2. **`def-cofinality`** — the bold heading "Only one notion of 'cofinal' exists in this library" is falsified by `def-subnet` (which *defines* "eventually cofinal", cited by three items) and `def-archimedean-field` (bolds **cofinal** for ordered fields). The paragraph beneath it is correct and page-local; the heading overstates it — the "heading asserts more than the text gives" class.

3. **`ex-the-cardinality-of-the-continuum`** — "The one constraint proved in this development" undercounts. `ex-aleph-one-is-at-most-the-continuum`, same page, same commit, citing this very item, proves 2^ℵ₀ = ℵ_α with α ≥ 1. Same class as A8-4, one page over.

Chronology matters here: only **#2 is true published-claim decay** (`def-subnet`, 2026-07-31, postdates it). #1 and #3 were false the day they were written, #1 against a dependency the item itself declares — that indicts authoring-time verification rather than the corpus shifting under a true claim, and I've separated them in the receipt for A10.

